      "source_text": "The ``only if'' direction is clear.  Conversely, assume there exists a\nmorphism <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002>.\nNote that <MATH_0003> is a ring map compatible\nwith the map <MATH_0004>. Hence we obtain\n<MATH_0005>\nChoose a pushforward <MATH_0006>. By construction we can factor\n<MATH_0007> as <MATH_0008>. Moreover, as <MATH_0009>\nis a section of <MATH_0010>, we get a morphism\n<MATH_0011> such that <MATH_0012> is <MATH_0013>.\nBecause <MATH_0014> we find that the diagram\n<MATH_0015>\nis commutative. Hence by (S2) we obtain a morphism <MATH_0016>\nsuch that <MATH_0017> is the given map <MATH_0018>.\nThe solution to the problem is now to take <MATH_0019> equal to\nthe composition <MATH_0020>.\n",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
